# File: tests/features/image-input.feature
# Generated from: specs/35-read-image-input-support-from-each-provider-s-own-model-data/requirements.md
Feature: Image input support from each provider's own model data

  @SCN001
  Scenario: A ClinePass image model receives an image
    Given ClinePass's model data lists "moonshotai/kimi-k3" with image input and the recommended list offers "cline-pass/kimi-k3"
    When the catalog refreshes and a routed turn to "cline-pass/kimi-k3" carries an image
    Then the model is marked vision, its hub detail shows "vision", and the request carries the image

  @SCN002
  Scenario: An xAI image model is marked vision
    Given xAI's language-model data lists "grok-4.6" with image input
    When the catalog refreshes
    Then "xai/grok-4.6" is marked vision

  @SCN003
  Scenario: An OpenAI-compatible list states its modalities
    Given a custom provider lists one model with "input_modalities" ["text", "image"] and one with ["text"]
    When the catalog refreshes
    Then the first is marked vision and the second text-only

  @SCN004
  Scenario: OpenCode Go models carry bundled image support
    Given OpenCode Go lists "kimi-k3" and "glm-5.3"
    When the catalog refreshes
    Then "opencode-go/kimi-k3" is marked vision and "opencode-go/glm-5.3" text-only

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A text-only model gets the omission note
    Given "cline-pass/glm-5.3" is text-only
    When a routed turn to it carries an image
    Then the image is replaced with "(image omitted: cline-pass/glm-5.3 has no image input)" and the turn completes

  @SCN006
  Scenario: A failed capability lookup leaves the catalog working
    Given ClinePass's model data request answers HTTP 500
    When the catalog refreshes
    Then ClinePass's status is "ok" and its models are listed with image support from the remaining sources
